# WeCooked mobile — public runtime configuration.
#
# Copy this file to .env and adjust for your machine. .env is gitignored.
# ONLY EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are exposed to the app, and they are bundled into
# the shipped app — treat everything here as public. Never put a secret
# (API key, OAuth client secret, DB URI, JWT signing secret) in this file.

# --- Backend REST API -------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the WeCooked API (apps/api). The app appends "/api/v1" itself,
# so either form works:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:5000
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:5000/api/v1
#
# When this is unset, the app falls back to a local default per platform:
#   - iOS simulator / web : http://localhost:5000
#   - Android emulator     : http://10.0.2.2:5000   (emulator alias for the host)
#
# A PHYSICAL phone can reach NEITHER default — "localhost" on the phone is the
# phone, not your laptop. Point it at your computer's LAN address (shown in the
# Expo CLI output, or `ipconfig` / `ifconfig`), make sure apps/api is listening
# on that interface, and that your firewall allows the port. Phone and computer
# must be on the same network.
#
# The API URL is not a secret. It is only listed here so non-default setups
# (physical device, staging) can override it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# --- Google sign-in --------------------------------------------------------
# DEFERRED for now. The backend has no Google-auth endpoint yet, so the mobile
# Google button is intentionally disabled and the app performs no Google OAuth.
# No Google client id or secret is read by the app anymore. When backend Google
# auth lands it will be an ID-token exchange handled server-side — do not add an
# OAuth client secret here (EXPO_PUBLIC_* is not secret).
